# Rust build artifacts
/target
# The client lives in its own cargo workspace (crates/client-app) with its own
# target dir; ignore it too (the root `/target` only covers the server workspace).
/crates/client-app/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Local demo staging (built .exe binaries + demo data) — not source, never committed
/dist/

# Frontend redesign drops + scratch handed in/out during UI work
/maxsecu-frontend*.zip
/clipboard-*.png
/install-design.ps1

# Never commit secrets. The Dropbox token / app secret and the offline D5/D6
# key material are injected at runtime / kept air-gapped (DESIGN.md §16.6,
# stack.md §5.1) — they must never land in the repo.
*.secret
*.token
secrets/
.env
.env.*

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Reproducible-build scratch dirs (scripts/reproducible-build.*)
target-repro-a/
target-repro-b/

# Storage-audit scratch: the copied exe + ProcMon captures (.pml/.csv) are large
# runtime artifacts, and the Sysinternals ProcMon binaries are a downloaded tool —
# never source, never committed. (The audit SCRIPT under tools/storage-audit IS.)
/.audit-run/
/ProcessMonitor/

# Brainstorming visual-companion scratch (superpowers)
.superpowers/

# Vendored static ffmpeg for the universal-video-ingest feature (D-1). The binary
# is FETCHED (scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.ps1) and its SHA-256 is pinned in source
# (vendor/ffmpeg/README.md + crates/client-app/src/ffmpeg_bin.rs); the bytes
# themselves are never committed.
/vendor/ffmpeg/*.exe
/vendor/ffmpeg/*.zip

# Compile-time recovery-account pubkey PIN. Written by `maxsecu-setup` (T14) and
# baked into the client by `crates/client-app/build.rs` via a generated const;
# the bytes are a per-deployment trust anchor and are never committed. Absent →
# the build fails closed (or emits a labelled test pin under `--features
# unpinned-dev`). See `crates/client-app/src/recovery_pin.rs`.
/crates/client-app/recovery_pin.bin

# Root-level demo/runtime artifacts written by running the portable server +
# client (rerun-demo). These are per-run secrets and staging dirs — never source,
# never committed. The recovery/enrollment blobs are live trust material.
/recovery_key.blob
/recovery_pin.bin
/register.key
/.server-fresh/
/client/

# Scratch session handoffs under docs/ (`_handoff-*.md`). These are notes written for
# the NEXT session — environment walls, command sequences, loose ends — not documentation
# of the product. They go stale the moment the work lands, so they must never be committed:
# whatever in them is durable belongs in the design spec, the runbook, or project memory.
/docs/_handoff-*.md

# Offline-D5 ceremony artifacts, written to the repo root by scripts/install-client.ps1
# (maxsecu-setup defaults them alongside `--out $Root`). d5_key.blob / d5_recovery.blob
# ARE the directory trust root -- the air-gapped D5 secret whose public half is pinned
# into every client; directory_pub.der is that pin; connection_code.txt carries the
# server address + cert fingerprint handed to users. `install-client.ps1 -Reset` deletes
# exactly this set (install-client.ps1:129-137). Never source, never committed.
/d5_key.blob
/d5_recovery.blob
/directory_pub.der
/connection_code.txt
